From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:31:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] debian: let the ceph meta-package depend on the standard mgr
 modules

Up to Tentacle, ceph-mgr depended on ceph-mgr-modules-core, which
shipped all manager modules without heavy dependencies, for example
prometheus, nfs, iostat and snap_schedule. Since the split into
per-module packages, ceph-mgr only recommends these modules. Hosts that
do not install recommends, be it through the APT configuration or
because the installation uses --no-install-recommends, lose them on
upgrade and do not get them on new installations. A module that was
enabled then silently stops working, as the manager only raises a
health warning for missing always-on modules.

Make the ceph meta-package depend on ceph-mgr-modules-standard, which
pulls in the modules that ceph-mgr-modules-core shipped before the
split, plus mds_autoscaler, which the Debian packaging did not ship at
all before. Adding the dependency to ceph-mgr instead would create a
dependency loop with the module packages, which all depend on
ceph-mgr, and removing a single module would then also remove ceph-mgr
itself.

Signed-off-by: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
---
 debian/control | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/debian/control b/debian/control
--- a/debian/control
+++ b/debian/control
@@ -131,6 +131,7 @@ Standards-Version: 4.4.0
 Package: ceph
 Architecture: linux-any
 Depends: ceph-mgr (= ${binary:Version}),
+         ceph-mgr-modules-standard (= ${binary:Version}),
          ceph-mon (= ${binary:Version}),
          ceph-osd (= ${binary:Version}),
 Recommends: ceph-mds (= ${binary:Version}),
